<article class="env-lemma" id="0F2W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F2W">Lemma <span data-tag="0F2W">37.73.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a separated scheme which has an open covering by $n + 1$ affines. Then the affine stratification number of $X$ is at most $n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $X = U_0 \cup \ldots \cup U_ n$ is an affine open covering. Set 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X_ i = (U_ i \cup \ldots \cup U_ n) \setminus (U_{i + 1} \cup \ldots \cup U_ n)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Then $X_ i$ is affine as a closed subscheme of $U_ i$. The morphism $X_ i \to X$ is affine by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01SG" data-tag="01SG">29.11.12</a>. Finally, we have $\overline{X_ i} \subset X_ i \cup X_{i - 1} \cup \ldots X_0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>